        "original_id": "569fd69a-ab6f-57a1-8b94-b0225cf9f5d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Park, Christopher Sadler\n- Works: Creature Comforts, Wallace and Gromit, Shaun the Sheep, The Wrong Trousers, A Close Shave, Chicken Run, Rex the Runt, Cracking Contraptions\n- Concepts: stop motion clay animation, comedy mockumentary franchise\n\nFacts:\n- Creature Comforts originated in 1989 as a British humorous animated short film and later became a stop motion clay animation comedy mockumentary franchise.\n- The 1989 film Creature Comforts paired animated zoo animals with audio of people talking about their homes so the animals seemed to be interviewed about their living conditions.\n- Nick Park, born 6 December 1958, is an English director, writer, and animator best known for creating Wallace and Gromit and Shaun the Sheep.\n- Nick Park has received six Academy Award nominations and won four Oscars for Creature Comforts (1989), The Wrong Trousers (1993), A Close Shave (1995), and a 2005 work whose title is blank in the source.\n- Christopher Sadler is primarily known for his work on Wallace and Gromit, Chicken Run, Rex the Runt, Cracking Contraptions, Creature Comforts, and Shaun the Sheep.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
